Tuesday

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:42.040
{=0}June

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:42.080
Wednesday

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:42.080
{=0}June

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:42.120
{=0}June

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:42.170
Wednesday

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:42.170
{=0}June

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:42.210
{=0}June

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:43.580
Wednesday

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:42.250
{=0}June

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:42.330
{=0}June

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:43.580
June

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:47.760
Wait, you seriously yelled at him?

00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:52.100
I sure did! He keeps coming home
drunk every night!

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:57.640
Knowing you, Rena, you must've
given him a real stern talking-to.

00:15:57.640 --> 00:15:59.980
But, like, how can you yell at your <i>dad</i>?

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:02.270
Goodness me, Keiichi-<i>san</i>.

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:04.320
Forgive me my impropriety,

00:16:04.320 --> 00:16:08.110
but some familial problems
actually <i>demand </i>harsh responses!

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:13.290
I talked to his friend,
Rina-<i>san</i>, too, and she agreed to help.

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:15.870
Wow. You really put in the work.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:17.160
Thanks!

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:20.870
June

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:20.870
Sunday

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:33.010
June

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:33.010
Monday

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:38.510
June

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:38.510
Wednesday

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:50.950
Perhaps you just haven't realized
the true nature of happiness, Rika.

00:16:50.950 --> 00:16:51.990
Huh?

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:57.200
Painful moments, no matter how small,
stay in our hearts forever.

00:16:57.200 --> 00:17:01.920
But tiny moments of happiness
are quickly forgotten.

00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:06.550
Forget them, and you forget
how truly blessed you are,

00:17:06.550 --> 00:17:10.510
and you instead yearn for a happiness
far greater than you can bear.

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:16.470
I cannot think of a more
unfortunate turn of events.

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:22.060
You're happy now, yes, Rika?
What more could you possibly want?

00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:30.280
Please, don't ever leave us, Rika.

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:35.120
I'll stay here forever.

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:37.740
With my best friend, Satoko.

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:50.090
Why am I...

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:17.780
"Wednesday, June 22nd"

00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:19.450
"Thursday, June 23rd"

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:21.960
Isn't tomorrow...

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:24.660
DA VINCI

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:36.970
Rika! We should head home!

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:40.850
Okay, wait just one minute!

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:43.560
June

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:43.560
Friday

00:18:43.770 --> 00:18:45.100
Here it comes!

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:50.190
Got it.

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:52.860
Take this!

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:05.580
Satoko-<i>chan</i>! Stay back!

00:19:16.640 --> 00:19:21.350
Those memories again... but why?

00:19:27.440 --> 00:19:29.150
Huh?

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:31.980
Happy birthday, Satoko!

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:34.570
Happy birthday, Satoko!

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:36.570
Satoko-<i>chan</i>, happy birthday!

00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:39.530
Yeah! Here's to many more.

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:42.240
Ah...

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:45.960
Rika-<i>chan </i>put all of this
together for you!

00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:47.370
Here, look!

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:52.080
Get Satoko a great present
for her birthday

00:19:52.380 --> 00:19:53.550
Huh?

00:19:56.470 --> 00:19:59.970
I'm very thankful
for all of this, truly, but...

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:07.270
I know this day is really
hard for you, Satoko.

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:08.900
Nii-Nii...

00:20:08.900 --> 00:20:13.070
Still, I wanted everyone
to celebrate with you.

00:20:13.070 --> 00:20:16.740
Forgive me, I should not have acted
so presumptuously before.

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:23.540
A birthday spent
celebrated with friends...

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:26.200
Why wouldn't I be happy?

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:29.290
Okay, here's a present from me!

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:31.410
Everything you could ever know about veggies!!

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:31.410
Vegetable Encyclopedia

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:33.670
Okay, this one's from me!

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:35.670
It's soooo kyute!

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:39.470
Mion-<i>san</i>, thank you so very much.

00:20:39.470 --> 00:20:42.930
I have another present here for you, too.

00:20:42.930 --> 00:20:44.970
Goodness, another present?

00:20:46.770 --> 00:20:49.980
This was the most I could afford,
but I hope you like it.

00:20:49.980 --> 00:20:52.980
My, whatever could it be?

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:00.820
Huh?

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:02.280
Satoko-<i>chan</i>?

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:10.040
How did you know?

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:18.920
Please! A trap master like me
can spot a trap a mile away!

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:37.190
Up until last night, it <i>was </i>a trap,
just as you thought.

00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:39.780
But not anymore.

00:21:43.370 --> 00:21:47.490
Rika? Are you quite dead?

00:21:47.490 --> 00:21:50.580
I'll ask again.

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:52.370
How did you know?

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:55.710
There <i>is </i>a power that will
lead her to the truth...

00:21:57.960 --> 00:21:59.420
A miracle.

